# Windows reserved device name
NULdeployment-prep-report.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
public/data/version.json
scripts/game-integration-config.json

# Claude Code machine-local settings (permissions granted on this machine).
# The .local suffix means per-machine by convention; tracking it makes every
# permission grant a merge conflict.
.claude/settings.local.json
content_audit.json
page_audit.json

# Internal review builds. These live INSIDE the deploy root (public/), so they are
# one `git add -A` away from being published to pdoom1.com -- and two workflows
# (weekly-league-reset.yml, weekly-deployment.yml) stage the whole tree that way.
# Untracked is not enough on its own; ignored is.
public/_review/

# Agent worktrees created INSIDE the repo.
#
# On 2026-08-25 `git add -A` swept `.git-worktrees/platform-claims-render` --
# an entire embedded git repository -- into a commit, and it reached a PR before
# anyone noticed. Git warned about the embedded repo; the warning scrolled past
# in a compound command and was not read.
#
# Two ghosts were also found still registered days after their work had merged,
# and a separate agent measured 24 encoding-safety findings that were ALL inside
# a stale worktree left by another agent -- a check reporting real findings about
# files that are not part of the project.
#
# Worktrees belong OUTSIDE the repo (the scratchpad or D:/Local_Code/_wt). These
# patterns exist so that when one is created here anyway, it cannot be committed.
.git-worktrees/
worktrees/
*.worktree/
